# Files the course image build does not need.
#
# IMPORTANT: this file must stay pure ASCII.
# Docker BuildKit sends .dockerignore contents to the builder as the
# "excludePatterns" header, and that header rejects non-printable
# (i.e. non-ASCII) bytes:
#   ERROR: failed to build: ... header key "excludePatterns"
#   contains value with non-printable ASCII characters
# That is exactly what happened when this file carried Chinese comments
# plus a pattern ending in the Chinese baseline file name. Keep comments
# in English and avoid non-ASCII file names in patterns below.

.git
.github
node_modules
coderoad/node_modules
*.log
.tmp
.DS_Store

# Course content and docs. The image only needs the two coderoad
# manifests plus the baseline SQL under answers/.
TUTORIAL.md
coderoad.yaml
tutorial.json
README.md
CodeRoad*.docx
make_templates.py
sql
scripts

# Keep only the baseline SQL from answers/.
# Docker cannot re-include a file whose parent directory was excluded
# wholesale, so exclude the directory *contents* and then re-add.
answers/*
!answers/00.sql
